FGL(FormalSeries) -- constructing a formal group law
****************************************************

  * Function: *note FGL: FGL,
  * Usage: 
        FGL(s)
  * Inputs:
      * s, an instance of the type *note FormalSeries: FormalSeries,, in two
        variables
  * Outputs:
      * an instance of the type *note FormalGroupLaw: FormalGroupLaw,, 

Description
===========

This constructs an object of the class FormalGroupLaw out of a FormalSeries
living in a PolynomialRing with two generators. The axioms of the neutral
element, commutativity and associativity are checked up to the precision of s.

+-----------------------------------+
|i1 : R=ZZ[x,y]                     |
|                                   |
|o1 = R                             |
|                                   |
|o1 : PolynomialRing                |
+-----------------------------------+
|i2 : s = series(x+y+x*y,2)         |
|                                   |
|o2 = FormalSeries{x*y + x + y, 2}  |
|                                   |
|o2 : FormalSeries                  |
+-----------------------------------+
|i3 : f= FGL(s)                     |
|                                   |
|o3 = FormalGroupLaw{x*y + x + y, 2}|
|                                   |
|o3 : FormalGroupLaw                |
+-----------------------------------+

Ways to use this method:
========================

  * *note FGL(FormalSeries): FGL_lpFormalSeries_rp, -- constructing a formal
    group law
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

