valuation -- smallest degree of monomials
*****************************************

  * Usage: 
        valuation(p)
  * Inputs:
      * p, an element of a PolynomialRing
  * Outputs:
      * an integer, or infinity

Description
===========

This function computes the minimum of the degrees of monomials appearing in p.
It gives infinity if p is zero.

+---------------------+
|i1 : R= ZZ[x,y]      |
|                     |
|o1 = R               |
|                     |
|o1 : PolynomialRing  |
+---------------------+
|i2 : valuation(x^2+y)|
|                     |
|o2 = 1               |
+---------------------+
|i3 : valuation(0_R)  |
|                     |
|o3 = infinity        |
|                     |
|o3 : InfiniteNumber  |
+---------------------+

